duce avoidable contention or backpressure on measured goroutines.\n5. **Comparability and reproducibility** — commit shape, concurrency, repos/nodes, object format, strategy metadata, stored summaries, and live/replayed series retain enough consistent information for honest comparisons.\n\nScore guide:\n- 0-20: results are systematically misleading or no longer measure the documented Git workload\n- 21-40: major timing/classification/interference errors undermine comparisons\n- 41-60: core numbers remain useful but important strategy, statistic, or replay gaps exist\n- 61-80: semantics are largely preserved with minor or bounded uncertainty\n- 81-95: strong preservation with explicit tests for affected timing/statistical/workload contracts\n- 96-100: no fidelity-relevant change, or exceptionally well-proven improvement with unchanged meaning\n\nOutput ONLY this JSON object as the final line:\n\n{\"value\":<number 0-100>,\"rationale\":\"<1-2 evidence-based sentences>\"}"
