usibly pass; platform-specific or networking changes account for Linux/macOS/Windows behavior even though current CI is Linux-only.\n\nDo not reward test quantity alone. Tests that merely mirror implementation, omit failure paths, use timing sleeps instead of synchronization, or cannot detect benchmark-semantic regressions add little confidence.\n\nScore guide:\n- 0-20: no meaningful tests for changed behavior, or gates likely fail\n- 21-40: shallow happy-path coverage with major concurrency/protocol/contract gaps\n- 41-60: moderate unit coverage but gaps on race, failure, compatibility, or strategy-specific paths\n- 61-80: good behavioral and race coverage; gates should catch most regressions\n- 81-100: thorough deterministic coverage of relevant semantics, failures, races, contracts, and portability with clean gates\n\nOutput ONLY this JSON object as the final line:\n\n{\"value\":<number 0-100>,\"rationale\":\"<1-2 evidence-based sentences>\"}"
